{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts@L1","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts","span":{"start":1,"end":10}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts","span":{"start":1,"end":10},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:40cc4fa9af76c2daabb393d170e6d7b5c5042782eff7c827b07ae6a11be1f024","meta":{"text":"PL/SQL lexer (M10) — zero-dependency, offline. Produces a token stream with 1-based line numbers.\nPL/SQL is case-insensitive for keywords/identifiers; the lexer lower-cases the `text` of word\ntokens so the parser can compare against lowercase keyword literals, and preserves the original\ncase only where needed (identifiers used as names keep their original form via `raw`).\nSkips `--` line comments and `/* … *​/` block comments. Handles `'…''…'` string literals (doubled\nquote escape). Never throws on malformed input — it emits an `unknown` token and advances, so the\nparser degrades gracefully (capability-honesty, extractor-plugins §5)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts@L188","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts","span":{"start":188,"end":188}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts","span":{"start":188,"end":188},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:bd713b9203d074efd44f7012ab6586eb843cdf4be67685920417ae958c0f4429","meta":{"text":"One retained comment block with its 1-based inclusive line span + cleaned text."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts@L195","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts","span":{"start":195,"end":200}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/lexer.ts","span":{"start":195,"end":200},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:55c161a047283f59feb068c050d4a0d15f4cc9c5160bf61a23e3bcf08411773f","meta":{"text":"Collect comment blocks from PL/SQL source. Contiguous `--` lines merge into one block; each\nslash-star block comment is its own block. The leading comment markers (`--`, star-slash, and\nleading star) are stripped and each line is trimmed; the block text is the lines joined by `\\n`.\nNever throws."}}
